==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Idi:Ne]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*10 [[Idi:Ne]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 16.67~18 seconds<sup>500f~540f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*8 [[Idi:Ne]]s spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 12~13.33 seconds<sup>360f~400f</sup>.
*4 [[Idi:Ne]]s spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 6.67~8 seconds<sup>200f~240f</sup>.
*4 [[Idi:Ne]]s spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 3.33~4.67 seconds<sup>100f~140f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The stage proves to be a nightmare with the quantity of 27 Idi:Nes. Even with an enemy limit of 10 and other enemies taking up space, their sheer combined weight of fire will quickly demolish any formation if given the chance. If they push, Galactic Overseer Nyandam will destroy anything entering his range, and killing him before the Idis is generally out of the question as he has more than 1.7m health. Any units that are disposable or can outrange the Idi:Nes will contribute greatly to the fight, the former allowing rapid replacement while the latter rains down fire from afar for staying power. Feel free to bring any units of your choice, as unlike the [[Idi:Re|original Idi]] [[Eldritch Forces/Invasion|Invasion]], there's no rarity restriction. The Idi:Nes' [[Surge Attack|Surge]]/[[Wave Attack|Wave]] Immunities, however, can greatly weaken the effectiveness of units such as [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], and due to their extreme damage, traditional tankers will fold very quickly, while a majority of specialist meatshields are outclassed by their generic equivalents.

The key to completing this nightmare of a stage is syncing up the Idi:Nes and keeping things that way for as long as possible. Synced Idi:Nes will all waste their attacks on a single unit, whereas desynced ones will hit the player's frontlines repeatedly until they eventually punch a hole in the frontline. Any methods of syncing the swarm up will be invaluable, which are listed in the recommended unit section.

As noted prior, the [[Base Barrier]] renders the enemy base invulnerable until the boss is defeated, which happens to be the first Idi:Ne spawned. The bulk of the enemy units don't appear until after 53.33 seconds, so if enough DPS can be somehow accumulated it is possible to cheese the stage and skip the fight in its entirety. Doing so, however, may prove difficult compared to a normal endurance strategy.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] - Thanks to his Metal ability and the enemy limit, one Metal Macho can withstand 12 individual hits and briefly stall a single group of Idis so other units can be positioned better.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] - The backbone of most strategies. Thanks to its high speed and extreme health, Boulder, when aided by Research [[Cat Combo]]s, can block any number of Idi:Nes during its brief lifetime of 1.3 seconds when all other meatshields fail, buying much more time for others to catch up. This isn't fully foolproof if too many Idis spawn and overwhelm it, but well-timed deployments still allow groups to be stalled at once.
*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] - It is recommended to use Crazed Cat instead of Manic Mohawk Cat due to Crazed Cat having the same speed as Manic Eraser. Send them both when the other one reaches about half of their cooldown (When one of them is has half of the cooldown left, send out the other one, and repeat.) While setting up the process to sync up the Idi:Nes, these units can effectively stall them until the bulk of the Idi:Nes come out, which by then the process for syncing the Idi:Nes up should start.
*[[Paperboy Cat (Rare Cat)| Paperboy Cat]] - If you're able to tough out the [[Invasion of Poultrio|very difficult Brutal Advent]] this unit originates from, it will work wonders against groups of Idi:Nes. With its [[Insane Damage]] against Relic, Long Distance keeping them at a safe range, and multihit being able to knock the Idis back twice per attack cycle, this beast of a spammable unit is a fantastic choice for this stage.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - While not essential and sometimes even detrimental, Cyberpunk's Long Distance attacks can Slow the Idi:Ne swarms from pushing for 4 seconds when fully Talented, during which many more meatshields could be sent to stall them. To some extent this also applies to [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]], but there are simply too many Idi:Nes for him to handle.
*[[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|Superfeline II]] - Though its hard-to-obtain True Form is ideal for this stage, even a decently leveled Evolved Form Superfeline can help a lot to knock back and sync the attacks of a large group of Idi:Nes, dealing very high damage and making them significantly easier to stall.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk Cat]] - Very cheap to spam and with high speed, Brainwashed Mohawk's 30% Anti-Relic/[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] Dodge ability allows him to effectively stall any number of Idis and Doge Darks if it activates. Brainwashed Mohawk, however, is very hard to obtain from the gacha in the first place, although players who have cleared Revival of Origin generally won't have much difficulty clearing his [[Century's End (Merciless)|Awakening stage]].
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] and [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]]: Bulky meatshields against Relics, capable of surviving multiple hits from Idi:Ne at level 50. Not as spammable as traditional meatshields, however, but that can be fixed with the help of Research Combos.
*[[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] - As the stage is only available after [[Revival of Origin]], Ape Lord Luza can contribute greatly in the stage through its Long Distance attacks, as well as having Massive Damage/Resistance to [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] and Curse Immunity that can almost certainly stagger groups of Idi:Nes in one swift blow. It also outranges their Omni Strikes, but a dense layer of defense is needed to account for its lengthy recharge time.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] - Doron is significantly less effective here due to the Idi:Nes' Surge Immunity, but his 600-range Omni Strike and extreme health will usually allow him to apply a 6.67-second Freeze and Knockback, paralyzing groups of them to provide some breathing room by syncing their attacks to be wasted on weaker units instead of breaking through.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] - A rather weird unit to use that can see some very strong usage with proper Boulder Cat timings to ensure the bulk of the Idi:Nes don't hit her. Being able to sync up the Idi:Nes rather easily with Boulder Cat is her best use, but she can also deliver huge damage to the Idi:Nes if kept alive. If you are using her, it is important to understand how Naala attacks to ensure she doesn't get hit by the Idi:Nes. '''The first attack will only hit one of the Idi:Nes, while the second attack will hit the rest of them.''' Keeping this in mind is extremely important to know when to send out Boulder, for most instances it is recommended to either send out Boulder Cat after Naala lands the first hit or right when she's about to, depending on how far away the Idi:Nes are from the Cat Base.
*[[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Spiritual Yulala]] - '''Note that Spiritual Yulala needs to be at least Level 34 in order to consistently knockback the Idi:Nes in one hit.''' This stage seems to be an ideal place for Yulala's [[True Form]], whose Long Distance attacks can actually bombard the Idi:Nes with impunity through his Massive Damage to Relics. He may, however, prove inconsistent with his very high speed which can clip him into the Idi:Nes' line of fire, which can be circuvented through proper Boulder Cat timings as well as other meatshields. He will eventually get killed by Galactic Overseer Nyandam, but the amount of damage he can rack up on the Idi:Ne swarm if used properly will prove invaluable.
*[[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Mewtone]] - His absurd range and Omnistrike allowed him to easily synchronize Idi:Nes, denying her existence in process while his Conjure let you synchronize Idi:Nes again incase of an emergency and push Nyandam. Although he cannot outrange Nyandam, his 900 range Omni Strike can still potentially snipe Nyandam from behind the other threats.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] - Phonoa can outrange all enemies (barring Galactic Overseer Nyandam) while pummeling them from afar with Long Distance attacks that reach up to 1000 range, all while dealing Massive Damage to everything, as every enemy here has a trait.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] - Similar to their light counterpart, King of Extinction Phono stands at extreme range, with their attacks being able to reach up to 900 range. However, they trade standing range for an ability to slow everything they hit for 2 seconds, all the while dealing great damage on each of their three attacks. While their Mini-Surge isn't exactly useful here, they are able to get the swarm of Idi:Nes off your front line while chipping down the Nyandam in the back. Do be careful, however, as King of Extinction Phono is outranged by Nyandam if they advance too far (600>500), so it's generally advisable to only send them out if you're sure that the Idi:Nes will prevent them from moving into the Nyandam's range.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanagi]] - Although he seems like he wouldn't be of use here, his sheer damage at level 50 is enough to cripple a single Idi instantly and take huge chunks out of Nyandam's health in the back. He wont stay around for too long, however. Despite this, what makes him really good here is his conjure, which is capable of pushing the Idis off your frontlines and give you some breathing space.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Bad Blaster Saki]] - In True Form, Bad Blaster Saki targets [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] and Relics from extreme range (500-900, stands at 600) with equally extreme impact, which can dent huge groups of Idi:Nes with each successful hit as long as they and Doge Darks don't get inside her blind spot. She can also deal hefty damage to Nyandam. Her Strong Against talent is highly recommended as it improves her damage and survivability by a lot.
*[[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|CAT-10 Gigapult]] - If one owns this [[Ultra Form]], its newfound anti-Relic Weaken/Resistance, expansive Long Distance attacks and Curse Immunity can greatly hinder the Idis while chipping Nyandam, despite its very long recharge time.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]] - Admittedly, Lasvoss isn't as consistent as he would usually be due to his very high cost, 30% chance Savage Blows and small range difference (320>300), but when properly positioned, he can possibly kill an entire group of Idis, while his survive ability gives him a second chance at hitting them. Lasvoss also has a [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Research Combo]] useful for Boulder timing.
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]] - While Aphrodite is not the most powerful Uber in terms of DPS, her massive damage against Aliens allows her to deal massive damage to Nyandam whilst syncing the Idis making them a lot more manageable. As long as the Relic Doges and Doge Darks don't infiltrate her blind spot, she can be an alternative to Saki if you don't have her.
*[[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]] - Outranging quite literally everything in this stage, Piccolan can provide valuable crowd control if its hits land on a swarm of Idis, shutting them down completely and weakening them for a bit. Do note, if the Idis push, Piccolan Pasalan's sheer lack of survivability '''WILL''' get it killed.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]] - Being able to freeze both Idi:Nes and Galactic Overseer Nyandam, Salvation's Daughter Lunacia provides great support in this stage, especially because the Idi:Nes are susceptible to her [[Explosion]]s, and she can freeze entire groups of them at a time. Lunacia even trivializes the rushing of this stage.

