'''Battle:''' Start the stage by immediately sending out Can Can Cat to farm some cash from Doge Dark before spawning Ape Lord Luza. You need to hold the initial Idi:Nes at the enemy base until Luza can mosey his way down to the frontlines, where you can then push Galactic Overseer Nyandam back with the Breakerblast. While he's doing that, use Yulala to heavily cripple the boss Idi:Ne, as it poses a major issue since it can't be pushed behind the enemy base. Once you have everything in position, you just stall for as long as humanly possible. When Luza inevitably gets overwhelmed and dies, cycle out Yulala to sync up the Idi:Nes, and keep alternating between the two until the last Idi:Ne bites the dust. Your Breakerblast is an essential tool for occasionally syncing up the Idi:Ne horde on demand, and also pushing Nyandam backwards if Luza starts pushing too far into his attacking range. See XSkull walkthrough for more information.

