'''Battle:'''  Start the stage by immediately sending out Can Can Cat to farm some cash from Doge Darks, then lure the first Idi:Ne to the Cat Base and chain it with Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat and Cone Cat. He should kill her right as the second Idi:Ne spawns, before proceeding to chain that one all the way to the enemy base. Now, it's just a battle of endurance where you will work to maintain as much ground as possible whilst continuously chipping away at the Idi:Nes with Bargain Cat's Long Distance Multi-Hits. Bargain Cat narrowly outranges Idi:Ne, making her the perfect tool to completely sync them up in the event that the Idi:Nes start pushing forwards. Every once in a while, cycle out Awakened Bahamut Cat + Thunderbolt to get in a ridiculous amount of burst damage and replenish your wallet with the inheritance dropped by the Idi:Nes. Not only can the enemies seldom push forwards thanks to your insane defense, but your offense is extremely disposable and thus not as prone to getting obliterated at a moment's notice by Galactic Overseer Nyandam like traditional backliners.

